It seems an old usage. ta'u was inversely defined on the CLL, and Bob
LeChevalier says the latter is correct:
http://groups.google.com/group/lojban/browse_thread/thread/5c5b14ed350c5337
On jbovlaste, the English and the Spanish definitions are not yet
corrected, but the Lojbanic definition supports the CLL.

According to the current definition, the examples of ta'u and ta'unai sould be:

mi zdani platu .i ta'u mi platu lo zdani be mi
.i
mi platu lo zdani be mi .i ta'unai mi zdani platu

mu'o

